                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If u think this game has a scary villain by the thumbnail in it then you are in for a rude awakening.  Your niece has been captured by an artist who has the power to bring whatever he paints to life and it is your job to save her. \n\nPros\nMusic is quite good\nDifficulty slider\nNo Hidden Object warning penalty. Feel free to keep clicking till you find a object.\nMap was easy to navigate and traverse through.\n\n\nCons:\nSkippable cutscenes, I’d excuse this if it had a simple “skip” button but one accidental click and you could skip important dialogue\nMouths don’t move to match the dialogue. \nHidden Object / Hidden Object Puzzle sections could be difficult for newcomers.\n\nBuy this game on sale for $4.99\n",
